[{"id":"VRCE-4-30-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":1,"english":"Lakşmaņa again addressed his high-minded elder brother, the son of a king, influenced by passion, stricken with grief, and poorly, with the following words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.791,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23f6f5329b85af2bc5d12b6d3a76a70cafcb6e4fc07e62988a5a1317e0b4a9b5","compact":"36c7bc762fc6fc508bfb4893bfbe631f800fa8ed7c6a8db9e5cd3edbc09e5e14","nasal":"1d68ca3c2a5d415a90cef62a672ff3db0d3c0fc9434b8b5290a30cc3583e4a34"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":2,"english":"That monkey shall not follow the actions of the pious, shall not think of the great fruit (the accession of kingdom) reaped by our friendship; kingdom because he has not the right understanding to make good his promise.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.564,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c0d72a4337472f12f18db99f1cd499b53b763020c077f3fae9ff156e51d573e","compact":"167a9939f6a0bbb5d86e3f6bde6ac1bcab27ad9e1e6dc9df833082930b8e9da3","nasal":"5e7dec1290997bf838e5ed4df9c12e12c5f545d509cc883b9e3bf62a11dda76f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":3,"english":"Owing to the wane of his understanding in consequence of your favour he is addicted to rural enjoyments and has forgot to return your benefits. O hero, killed let him espy his elder brother Vāli. It is not proper to confer kingdom upon that wicked-minded one.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.478,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ce1e65437a5a72b85f6655834b9956857898e8e69adc6ece37597a773c46c0e","compact":"750952baed74d7888c217f7fac4ed79e71dfa501e439631527af00ace8d1392e","nasal":"750952baed74d7888c217f7fac4ed79e71dfa501e439631527af00ace8d1392e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":4,"english":"I am unable to bear the outburst of my ire forsooth shall I kill today, that liar Sugrīva. May the son of Vāli with other principal monkeys engage in quest of that daughter of a king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9e14cc48a7b356b1ba662bae91707bbfdc3505682197148cc8678548efe28fe","compact":"489c05e0a7608829be6c3a6f615dc0a445c30eb3dc1f65ac9121dbb4dffc2147","nasal":"7c23b1ac0e3adfe4009a57d90fa063e317dc2b1a23aca555e3c788d008ad9071"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":5,"english":"Beholding him rise up from the seat with bow in his hand and greatly wrought up with anger and hearing him thus announce his intention about the destruction of Sugriva, Rama, the slayer of foes, spoke to him the following humble words worthy of being spoken on that occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f71ebe86012b12b5267efda4e39c49517ed275a5422543436745a64a2552e1bd","compact":"477e90e87fc3c3788cb00a1cae9277e3024d7f2052bc7b73316f1472964db20b","nasal":"75d4949041998c475370a4e2d2e3437785211b5763358f73c55fd3994e4883e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":6,"english":"Persons like you on this earth do not perpetrate the crime of destroying their friends. He is truly a great hero and an excellent person who subdues anger by his right understanding, O Lakṣmaṇa, it is not proper for you to bring about the destruction of your friend, do you follow your former friendship and good feelings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd38178d8094154eb58106229f1a58ad43d48a064e159d0c0ad6a109d67f1668","compact":"5d00459be8241688f63f22083fcabf812734f940c38cc0f1f5c304044ba0864a","nasal":"5160ce297346ec5798c6abd36e636312a0d10e68bffdc5cb4521704fe9ceda9f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":7,"english":"Persons like you on this earth do not perpetrate the crime of destroying their friends. He is truly a great hero and an excellent person who subdues anger by his right understanding, O Lakṣmaṇa, it is not proper for you to bring about the destruction of your friend, do you follow your former friendship and good feelings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1af9d2c1b4cd18d2e25a6e93c6e8a012230257c9b0f79483e698809faa82648","compact":"54863699c517aaf48e6a11c6e6f0c41e3780d3578401e8c43f5de01f939a1341","nasal":"54863699c517aaf48e6a11c6e6f0c41e3780d3578401e8c43f5de01f939a1341"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":8,"english":"Avoiding harsh words do you address Sugrīva, who has violated his promise, with soothing words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a042fec32949852cadffac491ee5d255e5cedc0c22a13c32a20c9ee46f6efdb","compact":"65ef0fe21c8791968c5ba5fe17f97e762bc7a0b22784c41364bf2828f97a723b","nasal":"65ef0fe21c8791968c5ba5fe17f97e762bc7a0b22784c41364bf2828f97a723b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":9,"english":"Being thus duly counselled by his elder brother, that best of men, the heroic Laks maņa-the slayer of foes, entered the city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c74b37f6af57169299b04cc94a715454311f200dcc5977b3eda22e31d06b9ed","compact":"e8b594c9aeeb13ea1e136b13a65ada102d089b045fb4636310b9c23e423778f4","nasal":"e8b594c9aeeb13ea1e136b13a65ada102d089b045fb4636310b9c23e423778f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":10,"english":"Thereupon the highly intelligent Lakşmaņa of right understanding, and ever intent upon the welfare of his brother, taking up a bow like to Indra's, resembling the summit of a hill and terrible as Death himself, entered, wrought up with ire, the abode of the king of monkeys like the hill Mandāra.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a3ea02d10c50519e53b387f4a43d0cc24a2e649e0cd2bfced529c0ab2be9091","compact":"702c4cc3bbde1683de922a85641e366ddecdff152c5d2e8ccb197f0a6cd272e2","nasal":"702c4cc3bbde1683de922a85641e366ddecdff152c5d2e8ccb197f0a6cd272e2"}},{"id"