 with the fire of anger arising from the excitement of his brother's amour, and therefore displeased, proceeded quick as air.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"177e63a842cf6c80ee94abba4f32571fca9c845f2a614703853d84f03bd27a66","compact":"c110862dadda420f19f476a27a8029f0a7ede949260e9d6053cd3e06afbb51d4","nasal":"bd3cbe1fd85ef0ff4277c3d0133d9b859b416b7bdb31fe33052ef9a23eaff34b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":14,"english":"And on he proceeded, felling down by his velocity, Sāla, Tāla, and Aśvakarņa trees, throwing aside the mountain summits and other trees, breaking rocks into pieces with his feet and striding very quickly like to a fleet-coursing elephant.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.561,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3115099b682e2b90ac65f8391b314172687e3a51aa75bf26c05238151a3fc0ee","compact":"8a53bd4f3ff9a19a71bdb41080cf06cb0068596384fbf6f2a68cd4e96bfde8ec","nasal":"8a53bd4f3ff9a19a71bdb41080cf06cb0068596384fbf6f2a68cd4e96bfde8ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-30-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":30,"verse":15,"english":"And on he proceeded, felling down by his velocity, Sāla, Tāla, and Aśvakarņa trees, throwing aside the mountain summits and other trees, breaking rocks into pieces with his feet and striding very quickly like to a fleet-coursing elephant.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-31-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4030015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"s